---
import PlainSummary from '../PlainSummary.astro';
---
<section class="sec" id="module-01" aria-labelledby="m1-h" data-depth="0.3" data-scene="module-01">
  <div class="wrap mod__grid">
    <div class="col smudge">
      <p class="eyebrow">MODULE 01 · STUDY PROCEDURE</p>
      <h2 class="h2 recede-h" id="m1-h">Read the files comfortably.</h2>
      <p class="narr recede">Field staff are encouraged to explore the archive in their free time. To better facilitate this use case, Deepwell sets every article in Literata at a comfortable size and measure, the way a book is typeset rather than a wiki page. It is faithful to the source and easier on the eyes, built for the long, late night read that orientation inevitably becomes.</p>
      <ul class="feat">
        <li><strong>Set for reading.</strong><br/>Literata, generous line-height, a proper reading column — not a wall of wiki text.</li>
        <li><strong>Faithful to the file.</strong><br/>Footnotes, collapsibles, tables, and anomaly-classification bars all render cleanly and correctly.</li>
        <li><strong>Made legible.</strong><br/>Adjustable size and spacing, plus OpenDyslexic and Atkinson Hyperlegible for readers who need them.</li>
      </ul>
      <PlainSummary>Beautiful, faithful typography, with accessibility fonts.</PlainSummary>
    </div>
    <div class="mod__visual">
      <figure class="reader reader--sm" data-font="literata" aria-label="Reading view: a passage with a footnote, and a choice of reading typeface">
        <i class="reader__lamp" aria-hidden="true" style="opacity: 0.8"></i>
        <i class="reader__edge" aria-hidden="true" style="opacity: 0.8"></i>
        <div class="reader__meta"><span><span data-font-name>Literata</span> · 18 / 1.7</span><span>68 ch</span></div>
        <div class="reader__body">
          <p>The inventory was taken at night, when the building was quiet enough to count. Each drawer was opened, its contents named aloud, and closed again. The clerk wrote in pencil, in case anything needed to be revised.<sup>1</sup></p>
        </div>
        <p class="reader__fn">1. Nothing was revised.</p>
        <div class="reader__chips" role="group" aria-label="Reading typeface">
          <button type="button" data-font="literata" aria-pressed="true">Literata</button>
          <button type="button" data-font="atkinson" aria-pressed="false">Atkinson Hyperlegible</button>
          <button type="button" data-font="opendyslexic" aria-pressed="false">OpenDyslexic</button>
        </div>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<script>
  // The chips are the app's typeface setting in miniature: a pick re-sets this card's passage only.
  const FAMILY: Record<string, string> = { literata: 'Literata', atkinson: 'Atkinson Hyperlegible', opendyslexic: 'OpenDyslexic' };
  const fig = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#module-01 .reader');
  const name = fig?.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-font-name]');
  const chips = [...(fig?.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.reader__chips button') ?? [])];
  const warm = (font: string): void => { void document.fonts?.load(`400 16px "${FAMILY[font]}"`).catch(() => {}); };
  for (const chip of chips) {
    const font = chip.dataset.font!;
    chip.addEventListener('pointerenter', () => warm(font), { once: true });
    chip.addEventListener('focus', () => warm(font), { once: true });
    chip.addEventListener('click', () => {
      if (!fig || fig.dataset.font === font) return;
      fig.dataset.font = font;
      for (const c of chips) c.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(c === chip));
      if (name) name.textContent = FAMILY[font]!;
      if (!matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches)
        for (const el of fig.querySelectorAll('.reader__body, .reader__fn')) el.animate([{ opacity: 0.2 }, { opacity: 1 }], { duration: 220, easing: 'ease-out' });
    });
  }
</script>
